  "id": "COMPOUND:30122 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "Paeonidaninol A is shown to interact with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, a sialyltransferase enzyme that plays a critical role in the synthesis of sialic acid-containing glycoproteins. This enzyme is a known target of multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and [(1S,3S,4S,6S,9R,10S,11S,13S,14S,16S)-3-acetyloxy-16-hydroxy-13-(hydroxymethyl)-5,5,9-trimethyl-12-oxapentacyclo[11.2.1.111,14.01,10.04,9]heptadecan-6-yl] acetate, which both target SK-VLB. The shared interaction with this sialyltransferase suggests a potential mechanism by which Paeonidaninol A may inhibit SK-VLB, possibly through the disruption of sialylated glycoprotein synthesis. The evidence supports a direct, mechanistic link between Paeonidaninol A and SK-VLB, mediated through the sialyltransferase pathway. The consistent targeting of this enzyme across multiple compounds and its role in SK-VLB suggests that Paeonidaninol A may exert its effects through a similar mechanism, potentially offering a novel therapeutic approach.",
